---
// =============================================================================
// [R6 NEW PAGE] Privacy Policy
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// This page did NOT exist before R6 — the global footer has linked to
// /privacy-policy/ since early in the project, but the page itself was never
// built, so it 404'd on every page of the site. That is a genuine launch
// blocker (no site that collects an email address via a newsletter form
// should launch without a privacy policy), so this exists to fix it.
//
// IMPORTANT — what this is and isn't:
// This is a conservative, honest, generic policy describing ONLY what this
// specific site actually does (a newsletter email-capture form, standard
// hosting/traffic logs, outbound Amazon Associates and BookFunnel links).
// Nothing about a specific email provider, analytics tool, or data-retention
// practice is asserted beyond what's true of the current build. This is NOT a
// substitute for review by a qualified attorney — flagged clearly in
// R6-Launch-Readiness-Report.md as something Tyler/Tiffany should have
// reviewed before (or shortly after) launch, same as most small-business
// sites launch with a reasonable starting policy and refine it. See the
// [R6.1 UPDATE] The one placeholder this page needed — a contact email —
// is now filled in with the address Tyler supplied (tiffanynoellechacon@gmail.com),
// also used on the new /contact/ page. No other content below was changed.
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const CONTACT_EMAIL = "tiffanynoellechacon@gmail.com";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Tiffany Noelle Chacon"
  description="How this website handles the information it collects."
>
  <section class="section legal">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow legal__content">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal__updated">Last updated: August 2026</p>

      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains what information this website collects, how it's used, and the choices you
        have. It applies to tiffanynoellechacon.com only.
      </p>

      <h2>Information You Provide</h2>
      <p>
        If you sign up for the newsletter, we collect the email address you provide. It's used to send you the
        content you signed up for — a free book, new release announcements, and occasional updates — and nothing
        else. We don't sell, rent, or trade your email address to anyone.
      </p>
      <p>Every newsletter email includes an unsubscribe link, and you can opt out at any time.</p>

      <h2>Information Collected Automatically</h2>
      <p>
        Like most websites, this site's hosting provider automatically logs standard technical information when you
        visit — things like your browser type, general device information, and which pages were viewed — for basic
        security and reliability purposes. This site does not use tracking cookies for advertising.
      </p>

      <h2>Links to Other Sites</h2>
      <p>
        This site links out to third-party retailers and services, including Amazon and BookFunnel, to sell or
        deliver books. As an Amazon Associate, Tiffany earns from qualifying purchases made through those links.
        Once you leave this site, that retailer's own privacy policy applies — this policy doesn't cover their
        practices.
      </p>

      <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>This site is not directed at children under 13, and does not knowingly collect information from them.</p>

      <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        This policy may be updated from time to time as the site changes. The "Last updated" date above will reflect
        any changes.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy or your information? Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding-block: var(--space-2xl);
  }
  .legal__content h1 {
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: var(--step-4);
    margin-block: var(--space-2xs) var(--space-2xs);
  }
  .legal__updated {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }
  .legal__content h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    margin-block: var(--space-xl) var(--space-xs);
  }
  .legal__content p {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    max-width: 68ch;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }
  .legal__content a {
    color: var(--color-tiffany-text);
  }
</style>
